{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering","id":1558301,"title":"Homebrew rules you like or are considering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-13T18:00:05-08:00","id":1558301,"title":"Homebrew rules you like or are considering","content":"Write homebrew rules you like.<br /> <br /> Probably also the edition.<br /> <br /> For V20<br /> <br /> Dexterity godstat<br /> Split up to hit rolls from dexterity, strength for brawl and perception for firearms. Lifted from bloodlines.<br /> Note: this makes potence stronger so optionally nerf that. Otherwise I like it.<br /> <br /> Rationale: Dexterity is well known to be an overloaded stat.It's still plenty useful outside this.<br /> <br /> More usage for blush of life:<br /> Blush of life lasts until the vampire falls asleep, torpors, dies (obviously), rotshreks, frenzies or takes aggravated damage from sunlight.<br /> <br /> Rationale: It's really annoying starting a scene with 'um so, who uses blush of life' especially if I have many social scenes. Here I can just ask at the start of the session and if it drops. V20 have it cost 8-humanity so usually 1-3 blood. I like to encourage blood expenditure and ironically this feels like more would use it.<br /> <br /> Dropping the blush in sunlight is just because I like the flavor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T23:29:44-08:00","id":1558339,"title":"","content":"I think everyone changes stuff for combat in V20. I prefer V20 over other editions (even revised), but the only thing i really preferred in V5 is combat. If there were a cool simplified way to change the combat i would love to hear.<br /> <br /> Personally i never did the solo declare actions turn, i just find it so tedious and gamey. Just:<br /> <br /> 1. Initiative<br /> 2. declare and do actions together (highest initiative first)<br /> 3. Damage &amp; soak<br /> <br /> Obv. Additional attack sucesses add tot he damage dice.<br /> _____________________________________________<br /> <br /> Something i have been considering is a \u201cdefensive action\u201d as a side resource: once per round you may Dodge/Parry to subtract successes from the damage dice pool and you still roll soak afterward. Effectively, characters without combat Disciplines would have one offensive action plus one defensive action each round.<br /> <br /> This does add an extra roll, but it also increases the value of ganging up on a target vampire (JJK jumping in action <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). In practice, one attacker would often \u201cburn\u201d their attack to draw out the targets defensive action and a second attacker can then hit at full lethality (unless the attacker has extra actions via Celerity, i have thought about giving more defensive actions to people with fortitude instead and make potence unguardable).<br /> <br /> In a straight 1v1 (no major combat Disciplines), it shifts combat away from burst/alpha-strike lethality toward more consistent chip damage.<br /> <br /> It would increase the value of doge and melee skill, as it is always &quot;on&quot;... basically getting 2 rolls for melee for attack and defense. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-17T07:01:05-08:00","id":1558362,"title":"","content":"So, we used the streamlined combat rules from V20DA for a while, but it has a tendency to make attacks a bit all or nothing. It can accidentally drop someone at the wrong time, which works in some games, but doesn't work for others.<br /> <br /> As a simplified combat system, I eventually came up with the following:<br /> <br /> <b>Basic rules changes</b><br /> Health levels: 5 + Stamina (+ Fortitude)<br /> If your track is filled with bashing or lethal, you're at \u20132 but still conscious. If it's filled with aggravated, you're unconscious and in torpor if you take any more damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Turn order</b><br /> Roll Initiative once.<br /> No reverse order of declaration. Declare when your turn is up.<br /> <br /> <b>Attacks</b><br /> All attacks are opposed tests. You can choose to clash instead to both roll your attacks against each other.<br /> <i><b>Attack: </b></i>Strength + Brawl/Melee or Dexterity + Athletics/Firearms<br /> <b><i>Defence:</i> </b>Dexterity or Wits + Athletics<br /> <br /> <b>Damage</b><br /> Net hits + damage modifier.<br /> No soak. Just mark it on your health track.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Damage modifiers and tags:</b></i><ul><li>Unarmed: +0</li> <li>Light: +1 (knife, pistol)</li> <li>Moderate: +2 (sword, heavy pistol)</li> <li>Heavy: +3 (axe, shotgun)</li> <li><i>Tags:</i><ul><li>Brutal: +1 (dragon's breath rounds, chainsaw)</li> <li>Improvised: \u20131 (bottle, chair)</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> That's it.<br /> <br /> To add spice, here are some dials:<br /> <br /> <b>Actions</b><br /> Everyone gets one action, one move, and one minor action (opening a door, etc). Additional minor actions cost \u20132 dice each<br /> <br /> If you want to rebalance Celerity, you can let someone pay 1 vitae to gain (Celerity) extra minor actions per round, for the duration of the scene. Trade in one minor action for an extra move or four minors for an extra regular action. This is cheaper than activating Celerity every round, but obviously gives you fewer actions overall. If you don't take one or more of your bonus minor actions, you still get the +1 Dexterity bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Clashes</b><br /> If someone attacks you, you can oppose with your own action, even if it's not an attack or defence (within reason). This is useful for non-combatants. Highest roll wins. A draw is a hard choice (player chooses): either both sides win, or both sides lose.<br /> <br /> <b>Delayed actions</b><br /> Delay to interrupt someone else's action later if you want to (then your actions happen simultaneously).<br /> <br /> <b>Simplified damage</b><br /> Cainites treat all mundane damage as bashing, magical/supernatural damage as lethal (including teeth and claws), and only fire, sunlight and True Faith as aggravated. No need to check Discipline powers and whatnot\u2014these rules override those. Protean 2 now only does lethal to Kindred, but mortals still take aggravated.<br /> <br /> For simplified task resolution, we do the following:<ul><li>Target numbers are fixed at 7+</li> <li>10s count twice and 1s do nothing</li> <li>A botch is a failure with one or more 1s</li> <li>+1 difficulty becomes \u20131 die</li> <li>\u20131 difficulty becomes +1 die</li> <li>1 success (marginal success in the V20 CRB) counts as success at a cost. 2 is a standard success with no drawbacks.</li> <li>If you run out of dice, either you can't roll, or you roll a chance die (1 = botch, 2\u20139 = failure, 10 = 1 success).</li> </ul>And that's it. It's very simple on the fly. It's basically <i>Exalted</i>'s core resolution with <i>Requiem</i>'s system for modifiers. We opted for that over increasing successes for difficulty because VTM works on a smaller scale than <i>Exalted</i>. A dice pool of 4 is about average, netting you 2 successes (a standard success). Losing a die is about half as bad as requiring them to roll an extra success (worth ~2 dice), so difficulties don't spiral quite as quickly. Also, it means you only have one moveable factor: number of dice. The target number and degree of success are always the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 02-17-2026, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T15:58:30-08:00","id":1558423,"title":"","content":"A house rule my current ST implemented which I now love.<br /> <br /> To teach a Discipline (proper Disciplines, not Blood Sorcery) to another Cainite, the teacher has to have the Discipline as In-Clan.<br /> <br /> e.g. a Tzimisce with Animalism 3 can teach Animalism 1-3 to anyone, but a Brujah with Animalism 3 can't pass on the gift.<br /> <br /> When I saw it, I thought it was kinda pointless, but then I got the idea. If you are running a longstanding game, West Marches, Living World etc. what winds up happening is a Mytherceria Plague spreads. It only has to be learnt once, and then it can just be passed around like... a sourdough starter, say.<br /> <br /> What it means is that a Brujah with Protean 2 is dangerous, and enviable, but their existence isn't a threat to the supernatural power of the city's Gangrel, as only the Gangrel can teach Protean, generally speaking. That Brujah also won't be able to learn Protean 3 and beyond without receiving demonstration in the powers and studying under someone who has them.<br /> <br /> It also just makes the setting make more sense, because while there might be a few Elders from before the Salubri genocide with Valeren, they can't pass it on, so the gift CAN die out. No Salubri, no Valeren being taught. Similarly, ancient Tremere with Vicissitude or Valeren can exist, but they won't be passing it down to others in the House.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T16:38:20-08:00","id":1558601,"title":"","content":"This might be a QoL houserule, but I don't like the idea of players losing control of their character to the ST during Frenzy.<br /> <br /> If the player is willing to accept they have temporarily become a Murder Hobo, I'd allow them to retain control of their characters while they act out the scene.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T13:58:59-07:00","id":1558773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1558423#post1558423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A house rule my current ST implemented which I now love.<br /> <br /> To teach a Discipline (proper Disciplines, not Blood Sorcery) to another Cainite, the teacher has to have the Discipline as In-Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this rule for the flavor, though I don't think I'll ever run a campaign where that would be an issue.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T03:02:47-07:00","id":1558849,"title":"","content":"Some that I would consider for character Generation in older Editions of the game (I'm not familiar with V5):<ul><li>fixed Starting Generation (at no cost) and no Generation Background</li> <li>higher Starting Willpower (something like Courage +3)</li> <li>Maybe also a couple of extra points for abilities and an additional point in virtures</li> <li>Using Dark Age Roads in the modern setting</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-17T21:26:13-07:00","id":1558915,"title":"","content":"One homebrew rule I have used for years and years is to tone down aggravated damage significantly. How exactly I\u2019ve done it has varied over the years. One variant is that only fire, sunlight, and faith deal aggravated damage. Often I combine that with making all normal non-magical damage bashing, supernatural damage (fangs, claws, etc.) lethal; and fire, sunlight, and faith deal aggravated damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T08:25:15-07:00","id":1558960,"title":"","content":"Regardless of their age or Humanity rating, I like to have all vampires instantly turn to ashes upon final death.<br /> <br /> It's cooler that way, and it pays homage to many other classic vampire series that have the monsters just instantly dissolve after getting stakes or beheaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T18:50:24-07:00","id":1558966,"title":"","content":"One i use for character's xp is that they gather it up to 10points, after that they convert them into 1 perk point that they can put wherever they want on their sheet (as long as it's justified). At character creation they have 10 perk points to complete their character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T13:19:58-07:00","id":1559017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1558915#post1558915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One homebrew rule I have used for years and years is to tone down aggravated damage significantly. How exactly I\u2019ve done it has varied over the years. One variant is that only fire, sunlight, and faith deal aggravated damage. Often I combine that with making all normal non-magical damage bashing, supernatural damage (fangs, claws, etc.) lethal; and fire, sunlight, and faith deal aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I do, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-02T12:58:38-07:00","id":1559186,"title":"","content":"Kindred being able to adapt to using technology for tools to better aid in their survival or an extension of specific interests such as Karsh keeping up with the advancement of military technology as the Warlord of the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-02T21:33:17-07:00","id":1559191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559186#post1559186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred being able to adapt to using technology for tools to better aid in their survival or an extension of specific interests such as Karsh keeping up with the advancement of military technology as the Warlord of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd rule it as only clan Brujah having the capacity for innovation. Their entire reputation was built around them being the clan of visionaries, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> For me, every other clan would become mentally stagnant and refuse to grow beyond whatever era they were embraced in. Which is why the clan elders would be so woefully out of touch with the world and need to bring in new blood to compensate for lack of understanding.<br /> <br /> It would also emphasize vampirism is meant to be a CURSE, as you are stuck watching the world change around you. Your generation dies out, your culture evolves, your society changes, your nation inevitably collapses. But throughout it all, you're still clinging to a version of the world that no longer exists. You are immortal, and immortality is a curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 04-03-2026, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T00:24:50-07:00","id":1559193,"title":"","content":"If someone like Sasha from the Tzsimce clan who is over a thousand years old can keep up with the times then so can the others","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T00:30:07-07:00","id":1559194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559191#post1559191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'd rule it as only clan Brujah having the capacity for innovation. Their entire reputation was built around them being the clan of visionaries, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> For me, every other clan would become mentally stagnant and refuse to grow beyond whatever era they were embraced in. Which is why the clan elders would be so woefully out of touch with the world and need to bring in new blood to compensate for lack of understanding.<br /> <br /> It would also emphasize vampirism is meant to be a CURSE, as you are stuck watching the world change around you. Your generation dies out, your culture evolves, your society changes, your nation inevitably collapses. But throughout it all, you're still clinging to a version of the world that no longer exists. You are immortal, and immortality is a curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds hard to apply consistently. It could translate into something like being unable to raise abilities after the Embrace, limiting vampiric development to increase in attributes and disciplines, but this would change the game a lot, and probably the disciplines, too. It would push vampiric society to be more concerned with embracing skilled humans than it is in the game's lore. I find it very interesting as an approach, if one is willing to develop it fully and produce new lore consistent with it.<br /> <br /> It may work better with disciplines rolling attribute + ability + discipline, like in Requiem. Clans would be strongly encouraged to embrace humans talented in the abilities that support their (un)natural gifts, but it would leave a path of growth for all vampires by investing in the attribute and discipline traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T00:41:27-07:00","id":1559195,"title":"","content":"VtM vampires can only increase their physical traits by spending blood and have three disciplines that directly augment physical exertion. Lore wise, their ability to manipulate society is the core of their power, even vis-a-vis other supernatural creatures, and yet the social disciplines are oddly limited or arbitrary RAW, especially Presence. Their longevity and paucity of material requirements make them perfect knowledge gatherers, but their lack of attunement for the spiritual (except specific clans) and the rules' lack of incentives to play hyper-nerds make that pathway unattractive for players and STs alike, even though you must expect powerful vampires to be very knowledgeable as well or else their power would falter, and elder paranoia means that trusting specialist advisors is not the strongest suit of princes and those above them.<br /> <br /> I am not sure how to improve the knowledge part, but it would be interesting if vampires were a bit different as creatures: if they could augment not only the body, but also the mind (mental attributes) and aura (social attributes) through blood and disciplines that improve social and mental dice pools like Potence, Celerity and Fortitude do. Their appearance and tendencies may change as well to reflect what they have invested on, with mental vampires becoming gradually more ethereal in looks, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T10:19:33-07:00","id":1559202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559194#post1559194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds hard to apply consistently. It could translate into something like being unable to raise abilities after the Embrace, limiting vampiric development to increase in attributes and disciplines, but this would change the game a lot, and probably the disciplines, too. It would push vampiric society to be more concerned with embracing skilled humans than it is in the game's lore. I find it very interesting as an approach, if one is willing to develop it fully and produce new lore consistent with it.<br /> <br /> It may work better with disciplines rolling attribute + ability + discipline, like in Requiem. Clans would be strongly encouraged to embrace humans talented in the abilities that support their (un)natural gifts, but it would leave a path of growth for all vampires by investing in the attribute and discipline traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, I don't mean mentally as in their intelligence or charisma, I mean mentally as in if you were a 90's kid at the time of your embrace, then your personality will always be that of a 90's kid.<br /> <br /> You can still become smarter, faster, stronger, est. but your cultural mindset would stuck in that decade.<br /> <br /> Hence why the clan elders are still carrying on like it's the middle ages and the American constitution doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T14:02:07-07:00","id":1559204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559202#post1559202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, no, I don't mean mentally as in their intelligence or charisma, I mean mentally as in if you were a 90's kid at the time of your embrace, then your personality will always be that of a 90's kid.<br /> <br /> You can still become smarter, faster, stronger, est. but your cultural mindset would stuck in that decade.<br /> <br /> Hence why the clan elders are still carrying on like it's the middle ages and the American constitution doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got your point, but my concern was how to apply it consistently because I see a lot of potential for conflicting interpretations on how it's meant to be roleplayed, and I find disagreements between ST and players can spoil the fun. Translating it mechanically can help make things more manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T15:07:45-07:00","id":1559206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559204#post1559204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got your point, but my concern was how to apply it consistently because I see a lot of potential for conflicting interpretations on how it's meant to be roleplayed, and I find disagreements between ST and players can spoil the fun. Translating it mechanically can help make things more manageable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well if Nosferatu can make do with never being able to raise their Appearance above 0, it shouldn't be too difficult to find a similar mechanic for the other clans.<br /> <br /> But yes, role playing it would require a bit of knowledge into how people viewed the world around them at the time. In some cases, that could be rather horrifying. Like, imagine being a vampire doctor, who still believes that your health can be linked back to the four bodily humors, or that mental problems can be easily fixed by performing a lobotomy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T23:20:52-07:00","id":1559210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559206#post1559206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, well if Nosferatu can make do with never being able to raise their Appearance above 0, it shouldn't be too difficult to find a similar mechanic for the other clans.<br /> <br /> But yes, role playing it would require a bit of knowledge into how people viewed the world around them at the time. In some cases, that could be rather horrifying. Like, imagine being a vampire doctor, who still believes that your health can be linked back to the four bodily humors, or that mental problems can be easily fixed by performing a lobotomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why tying the abilities in would make sense. A vampire who increases their Medicine dots is becoming more effective in curing people, which may reflect his having acquired new medical techniques compared to what was available in his time. That is, in fact, what led to the development of new medical theories and techniques: answering the problems and limits of the earlier ones.<br /> <br /> If we say that the vampire simply won't learn anymore, we can keep him operating at the same skill level and with the same framework and efficacy as before, except for the increase in attributes and disciplines. If we say he can improve abilities but is stuck with the &quot;mentality&quot; of his time it can be very confusing or require a lot of detail and creative thinking.<br /> <br /> For example: the vampire embraced with Medicine 2 in a time when the four humours theory or lobotomy are all the rage reaches, four centuries later, Medicine 5. We'd have to assume that he's managed to develop lobotomy or the four humours framework in such a way that it now actually works with the modifications he has made to the basic theory or techniques - and we'd have to invent what these modifications are. It's a bit weird and clunky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-04T06:18:46-07:00","id":1559213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559210#post1559210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example: the vampire embraced with Medicine 2 in a time when the four humours theory or lobotomy are all the rage reaches, four centuries later, Medicine 5. We'd have to assume that he's managed to develop lobotomy or the four humours framework in such a way that it now actually works with the modifications he has made to the basic theory or techniques - and we'd have to invent what these modifications are. It's a bit weird and clunky.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's how you get a crossover with the Sons of Ether! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T00:58:49-07:00","id":1559266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559213#post1559213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's how you get a crossover with the Sons of Ether! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>fair enough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T01:06:11-07:00","id":1559268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558301-homebrew-rules-you-like-or-are-considering?p=1559266#post1559266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> fair enough...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that sounds like a fun idea.<br /> <br /> Elders: <i>&quot;See, I told you fledglings you didn't know shit about how the world works!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Fledglings:<i> &quot;You told us Martians lived in invisible domes!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> SoE: <i>&quot;It's true, we built a radar that can penetrate their cloaking technology!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T04:56:51-07:00","id":1559521,"title":"","content":"Disciplines<br /> <br /> Fortitude-Fortitude comes with bashing auto soak per dot <br /> <br /> Celerity-celerity works like Potence but with dexerity<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy-Path of blood must be foundation path, other paths can be considered with GM approval<br /> <br /> Presence-Dominate gen rules apply<br /> <br /> Obfuscate-any supernatural with perception increases the difficulty by 1-3<br /> <br /> Clans/Bloodlines<br /> <br /> Samedi-Samedi disciplines are fortitude, obfuscate and Mortis-foundation path is graves decay<br /> <br /> Harbinger-in the unlikely event an lazerine embraces, the clan flaw is the cappadocian one<br /> <br /> Antrititru-any antitribu who rejects the Sabbat and humanity climbs to 8 reverts to old clan flaw<br /> <br /> Caitiff-A caitiff which diablerizes their way to 8th becomes a 'bloodline' Clan disciplines will be the three highest they have and clan flaw will be chosen from flaws or created by GM, all childer will inherit these traits<br /> <br /> Mechanics-<br /> Dodge and atheletics are merged<br /> <br /> At the end of session each player may give half an xp out to another player.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}